# Git push only on request

- Do **not** push to remote unless the user explicitly says to push (e.g. "push", "nupushink", "push i repo").
- Commit is also only when the user asks to commit — but push is stricter: never combine commit+push automatically after fixes unless they asked for push in that message.
- After finishing work, leave changes local if they did not ask to push; a short note that files are ready is enough.
- Pull/rebase only when needed for an explicit push request, or when the user asks to sync/pull.
